From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Subject: mm/memblock: preserve width of non-NUMA memory size
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:28:00 -0800

memblock_validate_numa_coverage() shifts the count of pages without
a valid node ID in unsigned long. On a 32-bit NUMA kernel, 4 GiB
of such memory wraps to zero, allowing an invalid firmware node map
to pass validation. The error message can also report a wrapped size.

Compute the byte count in u64 before both the comparison and the
diagnostic. The threshold remains in bytes.

Fixes: ff6c3d81f2e8 ("NUMA: optimize detection of memory with no node id assigned by firmware")
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: Mike Rapoport <rppt@kernel.org>

 mm/memblock.c |    8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/mm/memblock.c~mm-memblock-preserve-width-of-non-numa-memory-size
+++ a/mm/memblock.c
@@ -791,6 +791,7 @@ bool __init_memblock memblock_validate_n
 {
 	unsigned long nr_pages = 0;
 	unsigned long start_pfn, end_pfn, mem_size_mb;
+	u64 uncovered_bytes;
 	int nid, i;
 
 	/* calculate lost page */
@@ -799,10 +800,11 @@ bool __init_memblock memblock_validate_n
 			nr_pages += end_pfn - start_pfn;
 	}
 
-	if ((nr_pages << PAGE_SHIFT) > threshold_bytes) {
+	uncovered_bytes = (u64)nr_pages << PAGE_SHIFT;
+	if (uncovered_bytes > threshold_bytes) {
 		mem_size_mb = memblock_phys_mem_size() / SZ_1M;
-		pr_err("NUMA: no nodes coverage for %luMB of %luMB RAM\n",
-		       (nr_pages << PAGE_SHIFT) / SZ_1M, mem_size_mb);
+		pr_err("NUMA: no nodes coverage for %lluMB of %luMB RAM\n",
+		       uncovered_bytes / SZ_1M, mem_size_mb);
 		return false;
 	}
 
_
